[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Mastering Multi-Branch Pipelines, Pull Request Builders, and Organization Scans in Jenkins"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Automating continuous integration across multiple branches and pull requests is essential for modern software delivery. This tutorial explores how Jenkins Multi-Branch Pipelines, Pull Request builders, and Organization Scans eliminate the need for manual job creation and ensure rigorous code quality checks."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Understanding Multi-Branch Pipelines"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"A Multi-Branch Pipeline project enables you to implement different Jenkinsfiles for different branches of the same project. Instead of managing dozens of individual jobs, Jenkins automatically discovers branches, creates pipelines for branches containing a Jenkinsfile, and removes pipelines when branches are deleted."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Automatic branch discovery based on pattern matching."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Dynamic build execution using a repository-housed Jenkinsfile."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Automatic cleanup of old branch builds."},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Configuring Pull Request Builders"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Pull request builders allow Jenkins to automatically trigger builds when a developer opens, updates, or merges a pull request. Using plugins like the GitHub Branch Source or GitLab Plugin, Jenkins can report build statuses directly back to the code hosting platform."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"pipeline {
    agent any
    stages {
        stage('Build and Test') {
            steps {
                echo 'Building Pull Request: ${env.CHANGE_ID}'
                sh 'mvn clean test'
            }
        }
    }
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Implementing Organization Scans"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"An Organization Folder scan connects to a Git provider (such as GitHub Enterprise or Bitbucket Team/Organization) and scans all repositories within that organization or team. Jenkins automatically provisions new Multi-Branch Pipelines for any repository that contains a valid Jenkinsfile."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Navigate to Jenkins dashboard and click 'New Item'."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Select 'GitHub Organization' or 'Bitbucket Team' and click OK."},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Configure your credentials and the owner/organization name."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Set up periodic scan triggers to ensure newly added repositories are discovered automatically."},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"By combining Organization Scans, Multi-Branch Pipelines, and Pull Request builders, you establish a fully autonomous CI/CD architecture. Teams can scale their development efforts horizontally without incurring administrative overhead in Jenkins."}]
